{"id":"e4ea6a97-aa13-4463-ae45-5c1badc6cc25","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"ab099c339bf2d1aa","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/commands/git/git.ts","baseline":{"blob":"cdffddd61033ed0ae59fbefa579a15a1de712ea7","start":0,"end":53},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Juvy","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/util/juvy","\""]},"context":{"after":"291a4518e0376617"}},"payload":{"text":"The terminal's `git`: the workspace's one git (isomorphic-git, git-engine.ts — the same that Source Control and the\nreview panel show), spoken as git is: status, diff, log, add, restore, commit and branch, printed as git prints them,\neach a subcommand juvy routes and parses (command.ts). What changes the repository says so (`git.changed`), as git-service does, so Source Control and the review\npanel refresh.\n\n`diff` compares the working tree with HEAD: without `--staged` the files with unstaged changes, with it the staged\nones. A file staged and then changed again shows all of its changes either way — the index's own version isn't read.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:03:57.379Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:03:57.379Z"}
